{"title":"PDF to CBR conversion","description":"Install the rar program so a self-hosted Stirling PDF server can convert PDFs to CBR comic book files.","unlisted":false,"space":"server","layout":"","article":"<a class=\"doc-space\" data-accent=\"server\" href=\"/Server/\"><svg class=\"icon\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"3\" y=\"3\" width=\"18\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><rect x=\"3\" y=\"14\" width=\"18\" height=\"7\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M7 6.5h.01M7 17.5h.01\"/></svg><span>Self-hosted server</span></a>\n    <h1>PDF to CBR conversion</h1>\n<p>Converting PDFs to CBR needs the <code>rar</code> command-line program, which Stirling PDF does not ship. At startup, Stirling PDF turns the <code>pdf-to-cbr</code> tool on only if it finds <code>rar</code> on the <code>PATH</code>. PDF to CBZ needs nothing extra.</p>\n<p>RAR is shareware that needs a licence after its trial period; see the <a href=\"https://www.win-rar.com/winrarlicense.html?L=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">RAR licence</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"install-rar\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Install rar<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#install-rar\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><div class=\"tabs\" data-group=\"os\" data-sync=\"true\" id=\"tabs-0\"><div class=\"tab-list\" role=\"tablist\"><button role=\"tab\" class=\"tab-btn active\" data-value=\"linux\" aria-selected=\"true\">Linux</button><button role=\"tab\" class=\"tab-btn\" data-value=\"windows\" aria-selected=\"false\">Windows</button></div><div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"tab-panel active\" data-value=\"linux\">\n<p>Debian and Ubuntu have <code>rar</code> in the <code>non-free</code> repository:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><button class=\"codeblock-copy\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg></button><span class=\"codeblock-lang\">bash</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sudo</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> apt</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> install</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> rar</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Or download &quot;RAR for Linux x64&quot; from <a href=\"https://www.rarlab.com/download.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">rarlab.com</a> and copy the <code>rar</code> binary to <code>/usr/local/bin/</code>.</p>\n</div>\n<div role=\"tabpanel\" class=\"tab-panel\" data-value=\"windows\">\n<p>Download the RAR command line tools from <a href=\"https://www.rarlab.com/download.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">rarlab.com</a> and copy <code>rar.exe</code> to a folder on your system <code>PATH</code>.</p>\n</div></div>\n<p>Check that the account running Stirling PDF can find it (<code>which rar</code> on Linux, <code>where rar</code> on Windows), then restart Stirling PDF.</p>\n<h2 id=\"docker\" class=\"anchor-heading\">Docker<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#docker\" aria-label=\"Direct link\">#</a></h2><p>The container needs a Linux <code>rar</code> binary that matches its architecture. Mount one from the host, or build it into your own image:</p>\n<div class=\"codeblock\"><button class=\"codeblock-copy\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg width=\"15\" height=\"15\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><rect x=\"9\" y=\"9\" width=\"13\" height=\"13\" rx=\"2\"/><path d=\"M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1\"/></svg></button><span class=\"codeblock-lang\">yaml</span><pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">services</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">  stirling-pdf</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    volumes</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">      - </span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/usr/local/bin/rar:/usr/local/bin/rar:ro</span></span></code></pre></div>\n<p>Check it with <code>docker exec -it &lt;container_name&gt; rar</code>, then restart the container.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"doc-source\">\n      <a href=\"https://github.com/Stirling-Tools/Stirling-Tools.github.io/edit/main/docs/Server/Customisation/PDF-to-CBR.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\n        <svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M17 3a2.83 2.83 0 1 1 4 4L7.5 20.5 2 22l1.5-5.5L17 3z\"/></svg>\n        Edit this page on GitHub\n      </a>\n    </div>","toc":"<div class=\"toc-title\">On this page</div><ul><li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#install-rar\">Install rar</a></li>\n<li class=\"toc-l2\"><a href=\"#docker\">Docker</a></li></ul>","pager":"<a class=\"pager-link pager-prev\" href=\"/Server/Customisation/Mobile-Scanner/\">\n        <span class=\"pager-dir\">&larr; Previous</span>\n        <span class=\"pager-title\">Mobile scanner</span>\n      </a><a class=\"pager-link pager-next\" href=\"/Server/Operations/Performance/\">\n        <span class=\"pager-dir\">Next &rarr;</span>\n        <span class=\"pager-title\">Performance</span>\n      </a>"}